 "segments": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "s": 0.35,
   "e": 5.25,
   "text": "The dream of self-adapting neural networks is not a new idea.",
   "dur": 4.9,
   "voiced": 297,
   "sim": 0.695,
   "f0": 113.475,
   "st": -0.968,
   "range_st": 6.357,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "s": 5.47,
   "e": 9.62,
   "text": "In fact, it is historically older than backpropagation itself.",
   "dur": 4.15,
   "voiced": 214,
   "sim": 0.809,
   "f0": 116.707,
   "st": -0.482,
   "range_st": 4.271,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 2,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "s": 10.591,
   "e": 15.991,
   "text": "In 1949, Canadian psychologist Donald Hebb published The Organization of Behavior,",
   "dur": 5.4,
   "voiced": 404,
   "sim": 0.835,
   "f0": 121.475,
   "st": 0.211,
   "range_st": 6.594,
   "asr": 0.938,
   "attempts": 2,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "s": 16.112,
   "e": 19.773,
   "text": "introducing his foundational postulate of synaptic plasticity:",
   "dur": 3.661,
   "voiced": 251,
   "sim": 0.827,
   "f0": 118.87,
   "st": -0.164,
   "range_st": 3.509,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "s": 19.983,
   "e": 25.103,
   "text": "when an axon of cell A is near enough to excite cell B",
   "dur": 5.12,
   "voiced": 296,
   "sim": 0.652,
   "f0": 114.513,
   "st": -0.81,
   "range_st": 3.088,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 2,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "s": 25.356,
   "e": 27.796,
   "text": "and repeatedly takes part in firing it,",
   "dur": 2.44,
   "voiced": 172,
   "sim": 0.734,
   "f0": 117.938,
   "st": -0.3,
   "range_st": 5.506,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 2,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "s": 28.372,
   "e": 31.714,
   "text": "some growth process or metabolic change takes place.",
   "dur": 3.342,
   "voiced": 201,
   "sim": 0.804,
   "f0": 114.871,
   "st": -0.756,
   "range_st": 9.238,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "s": 33.164,
   "e": 36.103,
   "text": "In popular culture, this became the famous adage:",
   "dur": 2.939,
   "voiced": 215,
   "sim": 0.793,
   "f0": 118.384,
   "st": -0.235,
   "range_st": 5.163,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "s": 36.455,
   "e": 39.971,
   "text": "neurons that fire together, wire together.",
   "dur": 3.516,
   "voiced": 213,
   "sim": 0.693,
   "f0": 109.418,
   "st": -1.598,
   "range_st": 3.952,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "s": 40.596,
   "e": 49.676,
   "text": "In the decades that followed, mathematical theorists attempted to transform Hebb's intuitive biological principle into rigorous computational learning algorithms.",
   "dur": 9.08,
   "voiced": 640,
   "sim": 0.881,
   "f0": 117.709,
   "st": -0.334,
   "range_st": 5.473,
   "asr": 0.872,
   "attempts": 2,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "s": 50.754,
   "e": 56.674,
   "text": "In 1982, Finnish mathematician Erkki Oja introduced normalized Hebbian learning,",
   "dur": 5.92,
   "voiced": 423,
   "sim": 0.836,
   "f0": 122.352,
   "st": 0.336,
   "range_st": 5.774,
   "asr": 0.933,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "s": 57.002,
   "e": 73.116,
   "text": "proving that a single neuron equipped with local weight decay could mathematically discover the principal eigenvector of its input distribution",
   "dur": 16.114,
   "voiced": 249,
   "sim": 0.765,
   "f0": 125.986,
   "st": 0.843,
   "range_st": 5.962,
   "asr": 0.974,
   "attempts": 2,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "s": 73.339,
   "e": 76.725,
   "text": "without any external teacher or global loss function.",
   "dur": 3.386,
   "voiced": 221,
   "sim": 0.814,
   "f0": 118.642,
   "st": -0.197,
   "range_st": 4.486,
   "asr": 0.875,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "s": 77.479,
   "e": 82.127,
   "text": "Concurrently, Teuvo Kohonen invented Self-Organizing Maps,",
   "dur": 4.648,
   "voiced": 301,
   "sim": 0.813,
   "f0": 120.945,
   "st": 0.136,
   "range_st": 6.932,
   "asr": 0.714,
   "attempts": 6,
   "level": 3,
   "weak": true
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "s": 82.747,
   "e": 88.427,
   "text": "showing that uncoordinated, localized competition between neighboring units",
   "dur": 5.68,
   "voiced": 382,
   "sim": 0.843,
   "f0": 121.213,
   "st": 0.174,
   "range_st": 4.484,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "s": 88.732,
   "e": 95.844,
   "text": "could spontaneously fold a high-dimensional feature space into a beautifully ordered topological manifold.",
   "dur": 7.112,
   "voiced": 452,
   "sim": 0.852,
   "f0": 119.089,
   "st": -0.132,
   "range_st": 3.857,
   "asr": 0.963,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "s": 96.544,
   "e": 101.628,
   "text": "Later, researchers expanded this with BCM theory and Dynamic Rewiring Networks,",
   "dur": 5.085,
   "voiced": 367,
   "sim": 0.793,
   "f0": 119.026,
   "st": -0.141,
   "range_st": 6.722,
   "asr": 0.909,
   "attempts": 2,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "s": 101.819,
   "e": 111.211,
   "text": "adding structural plasticity rules where weak connections were pruned and new synaptic edges were randomly sprouted in response to local activity levels.",
   "dur": 9.392,
   "voiced": 611,
   "sim": 0.871,
   "f0": 118.083,
   "st": -0.279,
   "range_st": 4.754,
   "asr": 0.864,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "s": 112.33,
   "e": 116.994,
   "text": "The self-organizing hypothesis was breathtakingly elegant:",
   "dur": 4.664,
   "voiced": 281,
   "sim": 0.66,
   "f0": 117.385,
   "st": -0.381,
   "range_st": 5.496,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "s": 117.172,
   "e": 122.114,
   "text": "if we simply give a network the freedom to sculpt its own wiring using local rules,",
   "dur": 4.942,
   "voiced": 382,
   "sim": 0.79,
   "f0": 119.259,
   "st": -0.107,
   "range_st": 6.516,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "s": 122.255,
   "e": 130.335,
   "text": "general intelligence, modular specialization, and dynamic routing will organically emerge from the bottom up.",
   "dur": 8.08,
   "voiced": 507,
   "sim": 0.673,
   "f0": 115.033,
   "st": -0.732,
   "range_st": 2.712,
   "asr": 0.929,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "s": 131.035,
   "e": 134.955,
   "text": "For decades, this was viewed as the holy grail of artificial intelligence.",
   "dur": 3.92,
   "voiced": 290,
   "sim": 0.761,
   "f0": 119.465,
   "st": -0.077,
   "range_st": 8.101,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "s": 135.647,
   "e": 142.434,
   "text": "It promised networks that could learn continuously without catastrophic forgetting, growing new modules dynamically as needed.",
   "dur": 6.787,
   "voiced": 458,
   "sim": 0.81,
   "f0": 114.445,
   "st": -0.821,
   "range_st": 3.789,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "s": 143.134,
   "e": 147.706,
   "text": "Yet when these ideas were pushed to the scale of modern deep learning,",
   "dur": 4.572,
   "voiced": 347,
   "sim": 0.772,
   "f0": 119.603,
   "st": -0.057,
   "range_st": 4.346,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "s": 148.1,
   "e": 150.566,
   "text": "an unexpected crisis emerged.",
   "dur": 2.466,
   "voiced": 131,
   "sim": 0.686,
   "f0": 119.316,
   "st": -0.099,
   "range_st": 8.155,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 3,
   "level": 1
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "s": 150.786,
   "e": 157.791,
   "text": "The promised organic modularity failed to materialize, stalling in chaotic representational collapse.",
   "dur": 7.005,
   "voiced": 465,
   "sim": 0.856,
   "f0": 119.361,
   "st": -0.092,
   "range_st": 5.921,
   "asr": 0.833,
   "attempts": 3,
   "level": 1
  }
 ]
}